  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing Basic Education in the Philippines ABC+</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Philippines):  .USAID, through the ABC+ activity, supports the Philippine Department of Education (DepEd) to improve learner outcomes in reading, math, and socio-emotional learning, as well as help mitigate development impacts from the COVID-19 epidemic. USAID&apos;s work improves early grade instruction and delivery systems, increases access to quality materials, and strengthens education system capacity and commitment to manage and implement interventions supporting effective early grade instruction...Basic education-earmarked resources will fund the final year of implementation, which will focus on the consolidation of lessons learned and handover of programs. USAID will: consolidate and package its training programs for more coherent, accessible, and demand driven professional development (PD) interventions for teachers and administrators; integrate PD activities, including support systems like instructional support and leadership into DepEd systems; complete the joint training of pre-service universities and DepEd on education research; and pilot a mechanism for localized school-based training that is vertically supported with systems up to the regional level and through policies at the national level. USAID will complete the development of reading materials in Filipino, English, and 11 major Mother Tongue Languages for the covered regions. USAID will integrate the developed and tested tools, processes, mechanisms, and programs into DepEd systems. USAID will also support emerging priorities of DepEd including the National Reading Program. In the remaining months, the activity will conduct handovers and interventions to share the gains achieved and lessons learned. .</narrative>
  </description>
